    "diagnosis": "Questionable vascular invasion in a follicular tumour of uncertain malignant potential",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Sharply outlined collections of tumour cells covered by endothelium protrude and float into vascular spaces at the parenchymal interface of a well-circumscribed nodule that has a thin, poorly defined capsule. It is difficult to be sure whether intravascular tumour nests belong to the inside of the nodule and are therefore not to be regarded as evidence of vascular invasion, or whether the tumour nests are within the capsule and are therefore diagnostic of vascular invasion. The tumour cells lack the nuclear alterations of papillary carcinoma.",
