>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">FT-UMP</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3cm; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" nowrap=\"nowrap\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">FA</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">FA, follicular adenoma; FTC, follicular thyroid carcinoma; FT-UMP, follicular tumour of uncertain malignant potential; IEFVPTC, invasive encapsulated follicular variant of papillary thyroid carcinoma; NIFTP, non-invasive follicular neoplasm with papillary-like nuclear features; PTC, papillary thyroid carcinoma; WDC-NOS, well-differentiated carcinoma not otherwise specified; WDT-UMP, well-differentiated tumour of uncertain malignant potential.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Invasion</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> into vessels or through the tumour capsule (or into the thyroid parenchyma for well-circumscribed unencapsulated tumours).</span></p>",
